rice, in the right trade lane — consistently and profitably. Main Tasks and Key Responsibilities: New Business Acquisition – Heavyweight Express Proactively identify, target, and secure new business opportunities within the Ethiopia–China trade lane, with specific emphasis on Heavyweight Express shipments (30–1000 kg). Develop and execute a focused pipeline strategy targeting: Chinese manufacturing, industrial, and technology companies operating in Ethiopia. Chinese contractors, infrastructure developers, and project‑based investors. Ethiopian exporters and importers trading with Chinese partners. Leverage deep personal and professional networks within the Chinese business and investment community to unlock and accelerate commercial opportunities. Negotiate and close business in line with DHL Express pricing, yield, and governance standards, ensuring sustainable profitability. Conduct detailed customer needs, investment‑driven supply chain, and shipment‑flow analysis, positioning DHL Express Heavyweight solutions aligned to production timelines, project urgency, and service reliability. Convert time‑critical and freight‑like shipment flows into time‑definite DHL Express Heavyweight solutions. , insight, industry knowledge, and competitive positioning to win heavyweight express business. Work closely with Core and Retail Sales Teams to ensure structured conversion, onboarding, and accounting handovers. Build and manage a robust new China Ethiopia trade lane focused business pipeline through targeted prospecting, networking, and structured territory planning. Conduct in‑depth customer and shipment‑flow analysis to identify use cases where Express speed, reliability, and visibility deliver superior value versus forwarding alternatives. Develop and present tailored Heavyweight Express solutions, balancing global network capability, transit‑time commitments (on TDI – Time Definite International), cost‑to‑serve, and commercial sustainability. Negotiate and close new business in line with DHL Express pricing, yield, and governance standards, ensuring profitable growth. Coordinate closely with internal stakeholders (Operations, Gateway, Finance, Customer Service) to ensure smooth onboarding, first‑shipment stability, and structured handover to Core Sales for ongoing account management. Collaborate proactively with other DHL Group business units to support wider China–Africa investment‑led supply chain opportunities. Strategic Market Development & Stakeholder Engagement – Chinese Embassy in Ethiopia – Chinese Mission Embassy in Ethiopia. – Chinese Chambers of Commerce and business associations. – Investment and industrial‑park communities. Position DHL Express as the logistics partner of choice for Chinese‑backed businesses and investors through credibility, consistency, and visible engagement. Identify and prioritize investment‑driven industry verticals, including: – Industrial & Manufacturing – Automotive & Spare Parts – Technology & Electronics – Healthcare & Life Science",
