o documentation, timelines, and account status; Log and track client issues, delays, or discrepancies; Escalate unresolved issues to the Client Services Manager in a timely manner. Academic Requirements And Relevant Experience Master’s degree in Business Administration, Supply Chain Management, Finance, Public Administration, Economics, or a related field with a minimum of 2 years of relevant professional experience in client services, programme support, finance operations, project management, or supply chain administration OR A bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Supply Chain Management, Finance, Public Administration, Economics, or a related field with a minimum of 5 years of relevant professional experience in client services, programme support, finance operations, project management, or supply chain administration Experience working with public-sector institutions, multilateral organizations, or donor-funded programmes is an asset. Required Skills Strong organizational, administrative, and coo",
