    "title": "Team Lead-LIWAY Program - Readvertised",
    "organization": "SNV",
    "description": "SNV is a global development partner, deeply rooted in the countries where we operate. We are driven by a vision of a better world: A world where across every society all people live with dignity and have equitable opportunities to thrive sustainably. To make this vision a reality, we need transformations in vital agri-food, energy, and water systems. SNV contributes by strengthening capacities and catalyzing partnerships in these sectors. We help strengthen institutions and effective governance, reduce gender inequalities and barriers to social inclusion, and enable adaptation and mitigation to the climate and biodiversity crises. Building on 60 years of experience we support our partners with our technical and process expertise and methodological rigor. We do this in more than 20 countries in Africa and Asia with a team of approximately 1,600 colleagues. By being adaptable and tailoring our approaches to these different contexts, we can contribute to impact at scale, resulting in more equitable lives for all. Our core values of people-centeredness and respect, equity and equality, and diversity and inclusion, are fundamental to who we are, and what we do. This is reflected in our vision and mission, and strategy, which sets out our aspirations and commitments as our compass towards 2030. For more information on our operations in Ethiopia and SNV generally visit our website: www.snv.org Background of the Programme The Livelihoods Improvement for Women and Youth (LIWAY) is a thirteen-year programme (July 2017 to December 2028) funded by Swedish International Development Agency and the Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands. The programme is implemented by SNV and consortium of partners, with SNV leading the consortium. LIWAY applies a market system development (MSD) approach that involves identifying the root causes of market failure that disadvantage or exclude poor women and youth from wage and self-employment opportunities and identifying private companies and public institutions that have incentive and ability to deliver change. The aim is to make market systems work better for the target groups while demonstrating benefits to public and private actors that play a role in the systems to ensure local ownership and sustainability and continued improvement beyond the programme period. The approach involves experimentation and learning rapidly from failures and amplifying successes. Context and Purpose of the Job The Team Lead is part of the SNV Ethiopia and works for the LIWAY project funded by both EKN and Sida. The Team Lead will oversee the development and execution of effective system interventions within the anticipated urban livelihoods improvement program in Addis Ababa. This role requires strong technical knowledge in Market Systems Development (MSD), as well as leadership, strategic planning abilities, and effective team management to enhance overall performance and accountability. Job Description Lead Intervention Design and strategic planning Guide the development of market-based systemic interventions to ensure their efficiency and effectiveness in addressing system needs. Lead/co-lead the team members to design innovative solutions that align with project objectives. Ensure alignment of interventions across systems As required, facilitate specific interventions Develop comprehensive work plans and budgets that align with project goals and objectives. Ensure that system interventions are executed on schedule and within budget Monitor progress and adapt plans as necessary to achieve desired outcomes. Stakeholder Engagement Identify strategic partners/stakeholders. Engage with relevant stakeholders to gather insights and foster collaboration that supports intervention success. Build and maintain relationships with key partners to enhance program impact. Work closely with key market players, including government agencies, private business companies, financial institutions, and business development service providers, associations, business and/or sectoral associations to enhance their performance in market systems improvement. Steer interventions that require a higher level/policy level engagement. Facilitate linkage with other relevant programs within and outside the organisation. Team Management Coach and mentor Market System Advisors, guiding their professional development. Monitor and evaluate team performance, providing constructive feedback to enhance effectiveness. Facilitate capacity building for internal and external market actors. Steers colleagues and coaches associated partners/ external stakeholders on quality within the context of assignments. Provide technical expertise and guidance in MSD and apply process improvements in projects. Handle team performance management process according to the organization procedure. Coordinate Team Activities Facilitate collaboration among team members of partners to ensure complementary efforts and maximise overall efficiency. Organize team meeting",
